# The screenshot harness's sample PDF is written by hand and happens to be pure ASCII, so Git's
# content sniffing calls it text -- and with core.autocrlf=true a fresh checkout on Windows would
# rewrite every newline in it. That would move every byte in the file, and a PDF's xref table is a
# list of byte offsets, so the checked-out copy would no longer open. Marked binary so it is stored
# and restored unchanged.
*.pdf binary
